From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gerard Marull-Paretas <gerard@teslabs.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:52:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: input: touchscreen: hynitron,cst816x: Reference
 touchscreen.yaml

The controller reports positions in the coordinate range of the panel
it is fitted to, and how the panel is mounted varies from one board to
another. Reference the common touchscreen schema, so that boards can
describe them with the common properties (touchscreen-size-x/y,
touchscreen-inverted-x/y, touchscreen-swapped-x-y, ...), as other
touchscreen controller bindings do.

This patch was prepared with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude
Code, using Claude Opus 5.5), which wrote the change and this commit
message under the submitter's direction. It was reviewed by the
submitter, who takes responsibility for it.
---
 input/touchscreen/hynitron,cst816x.yaml | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/input/touchscreen/hynitron,cst816x.yaml b/input/touchscreen/hynitron,cst816x.yaml
index 72d4da636881..df52431b1d49 100644
--- a/input/touchscreen/hynitron,cst816x.yaml
+++ b/input/touchscreen/hynitron,cst816x.yaml
@@ -13,6 +13,9 @@ description: |
   Bindings for CST816x high performance self-capacitance touch chip series
   with single point gesture and real two-point operation.
 
+allOf:
+  - $ref: touchscreen.yaml#
+
 properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
@@ -41,7 +44,7 @@ required:
   - reg
   - interrupts
 
-additionalProperties: false
+unevaluatedProperties: false
 
 examples:
   - |
@@ -57,6 +60,8 @@ examples:
             interrupt-parent = <&gpio0>;
             interrupts = <4 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
             reset-gpios = <&gpio 17 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+            touchscreen-size-x = <240>;
+            touchscreen-size-y = <240>;
             linux,keycodes = <KEY_UP>, <KEY_DOWN>, <KEY_LEFT>, <KEY_RIGHT>,
                              <BTN_TOOL_TRIPLETAP>;
         };
